[["wrb.fr",null,"[null,[\"c_c64a8913836f68c7\",\"r_51cd9344c86f1737\"],null,null,[[\"rc_2853ada5b0815599\",[\"Analyst consensus for SpaceX's valuation by the end of 2026 centers in the **$1.35 trillion to $1.80 trillion** range, with an implied share price expectation around **$135–$180**. \\n\\nA breakdown of current forecast tiers highlights significant divergence based on execution, capital expenditure, and market liquidity:\\n\\n| Scenario | Implied Valuation | Target Share Price | Core Assumptions |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **Bear Case** | **$780B – $1.25T** | $60 – $95 | Multiples compress to 10–12x revenue; heavy Starship/AI CapEx drags margins; post-IPO lock-up expirations flood float. |\\n| **Base Case** | **$1.35T – $1.80T** | $135 – $180 | Starlink ARR scales steadily; launch cadence remains near-monopoly; consolidated 2026 revenues cross ~$40B. |\\n| **Bull Case** | **$2.0T – $2.67T+** | $200 – $280 | Direct-to-cell enterprise contracts scale globally; Starship commercialization beats schedule; premium multiple sustained. |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Key Upside Catalysts\\n\\n1. **Starlink Cash Cow \\u0026 Direct-to-Cell Monetization:** Starlink represents the vast majority of recurring, high-margin revenue. Accelerated adoption of direct-to-cell services (following the integration of EchoStar spectrum) and enterprise maritime/aviation agreements provide clear recurring cash flows.\\n2. **Starship Operational Milestones:** Demonstration of rapid Starship reusability, in-orbit refueling, and progress toward NASA Artemis HLS deliverables will derisk long-term deep-space operations and significantly compress per-kilogram launch costs.\\n3. **Space-Based AI \\u0026 Cloud Infrastructure:** Commercial monetization of orbital computing architectures and data networking contracts (e.g., partnerships with hyperscalers) could unlock software-like valuation multiples rather than standard aerospace hardware multiples.\\n4. **Defense \\u0026 Government Moats:** Dominance in national security launches, secure orbital networks (Starshield), and expanded NASA cargo/crew contract extensions ensure stable, non-cyclical revenue floors.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Downside Risks \\u0026 Valuation Drags\\n\\n1. **Post-IPO Share Float Dilution (Supply Shock):** Early lock-up releases and the impending expiration of the 180-day lock-up substantially expand the tradable float. A massive influx of secondary shares from early employees and institutions poses immediate downward price pressure.\\n2. **Capital Expenditure Burden \\u0026 Cash Burn:** Massive ongoing CapEx requirements for Starship test programs, satellite replenishment cycles, and data infrastructure threaten operating margins and free cash flow generation.\\n3. **Regulatory \\u0026 Orbital Congestion Bottlenecks:** Tightened FAA environmental reviews, FCC spectrum allocation disputes, and international resistance regarding space debris and low-Earth-orbit saturation could slow launch cadences.\\n4. **Multiples Compression:** If revenue growth decelerates or broader macroeconomic/tech multiples contract, an equity story trading well above historical aerospace multiples faces sharp multiple contraction.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Sources \\u0026 References\\n* [Sacra Research: SpaceX Valuation Analysis \\u0026 Revenue Scenarios](https://sacra.com/c/spacex/valuation/)\"],null,null,null,null,null,null,[1],\"en\",null,null,[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[],null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[null,[[[],\"Searched the web\",\"Google Search\",\"https://www.gstatic.com/images/branding/productlogos/googleg/v6/192px.svg\",[],\"Searched the web\",\"\",[[\"https://t1.gstatic.com/faviconV2?url\\u003dhttps://www.markets.com/\\u0026client\\u003dBARD\\u0026type\\u003dFAVICON\\u0026size\\u003d256\\u0026fallback_opts\\u003dTYPE,SIZE,URL\",\"https://www.markets.com/analysis/spacex-stock-price-prediction\",\"SpaceX Stock Price